{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>That YHWH may turn back from the fierceness of His anger.</b> He is the Elohim of Israel. And the secret of the matter concerning the seduced city is that its inhabitants were among those of whom the woman of Tekoa said (II Samuel 14:14), ״and devises devices so that none be thrust away,״ and so on — and behold, they are thrust away from the enclosure of the Holy One, blessed be He, and uprooted from the place of their root and their planting. Therefore Scripture obligated them to burning, in the manner of Korah, who was judged by burning; and all its spoil is forbidden for benefit, and that city shall be a mound forever — the souls shall not be rebuilt again for the revival of the dead, but shall be consumed in final annihilation." "<b>And give you compassion</b> — the attribute of compassion; and this is in the manner of what is written (Genesis 43:14), ״ואל שדי יתן לכם רחמים״, and understand this. And it says כי תשמע, in its explanation: כי תשמע בקול — when you hearken to the voice — which is YHWH your Elohim, to keep all His commandments, then you shall do what is upright in the eyes of YHWH, which is the distinctive Name, and this is clear."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:13.941882653Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}